      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely! Unions during the 20th century played a significant role in shaping the American middle class through several key impacts. By negotiating higher wages, unions helped workers accumulate more savings and consumer purchasing power. They also secured better working conditions, which improved the overall quality of life for many workers, ultimately contributing to increased life expectancy and higher education levels. Additionally, unions pushed for social benefits like healthcare and retirement programs, laying the foundation for the modern social safety net. Lastly, their efforts at fostering workplace democracy promoted principles of equality and fairness, which further contributed to broad-based middle-class growth.",
